WEBVTT

NOTE
StoryCast: When Everything Goes Wrong. Original explainer. Narrated by Mufaro, the creator of StoryCast.
Narration only; the video has no music or other sound effects. Timings measured from the recording.

1
00:00:00.612 --> 00:00:06.812
Hungary, August 1st, 2021,
a race nobody could have predicted.

2
00:00:07.692 --> 00:00:10.212
Rain has fallen at the Hungaroring.

3
00:00:10.292 --> 00:00:12.292
Lewis Hamilton starts on pole position

4
00:00:12.332 --> 00:00:15.852
with his Mercedes teammate
Valtteri Bottas alongside him.

5
00:00:15.992 --> 00:00:19.872
But in these conditions, the first
corner could change everything.

6
00:00:20.932 --> 00:00:23.892
And that's exactly what happens.

7
00:00:23.932 --> 00:00:27.232
Bottas brakes too late,
crashing into Lando Norris,

8
00:00:27.272 --> 00:00:28.892
who is pushed into Max Verstappen.

9
00:00:28.932 --> 00:00:32.152
Sergio Pérez is also
caught in the collision.

10
00:00:32.192 --> 00:00:35.752
Another incident involves
Lance Stroll and Charles Leclerc.

11
00:00:35.932 --> 00:00:39.452
Within moments, the race
has descended into chaos.

12
00:00:40.812 --> 00:00:43.552
The race is stopped,
but as the drivers wait,

13
00:00:43.592 --> 00:00:46.232
the rain eases and the
circuit begins to dry.

14
00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:48.332
A crucial decision is approaching.

15
00:00:49.832 --> 00:00:53.952
At the restart, every driver
behind Lewis Hamilton

16
00:00:53.992 --> 00:00:57.032
heads into the pits for dry-weather tyres.

17
00:00:57.152 --> 00:01:00.392
Hamilton stays out,
and when the lights go out,

18
00:01:00.432 --> 00:01:02.832
he's the only car on the starting grid.

19
00:01:02.932 --> 00:01:04.972
An extraordinary sight!

20
00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:09.212
Hamilton soon pits,
dropping down the order.

21
00:01:09.472 --> 00:01:13.292
Esteban Ocon takes the lead,
with Sebastian Vettel chasing him.

22
00:01:13.672 --> 00:01:15.912
Meanwhile, Fernando Alonso
battles Hamilton,

23
00:01:15.952 --> 00:01:20.672
delaying his recovery and giving
Ocon valuable breathing room.

24
00:01:21.372 --> 00:01:25.772
After 70 laps, Esteban Ocon
crosses the finish line.

25
00:01:25.872 --> 00:01:27.072
He's done it!

26
00:01:27.112 --> 00:01:30.412
His first ever Formula 1
Grand Prix victory.

27
00:01:30.832 --> 00:01:34.252
Vettel finishes in second on the road,
but is later disqualified.

28
00:01:34.472 --> 00:01:39.332
The official podium becomes
Ocon, Hamilton and Carlos Sainz.

29
00:01:39.952 --> 00:01:46.012
A race that began in chaos ends
with an unexpected champion.

30
00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:50.032
Sometimes everything has to go
wrong for history to be made.
